\begin{didyouknow}{Eigen Means Own}
The prefix \emph{eigen} is German for own or characteristic. David Hilbert used \emph{Eigenwert} and \emph{Eigenfunktion} in his 1904 work on integral equations, and the half-translated hybrid eigenvalue stuck in English. A real two-dimensional rotation matrix has no real eigenvectors unless the angle is $0$ or $\pi$. Its eigenvalues are $e^{\pm i\theta}$, a first hint that complex eigenvalues signal rotation.
\end{didyouknow}
% DYK-END

