\begin{didyouknow}{Jacobi's Rotations}
In 1846 Carl Jacobi published a method for diagonalizing a symmetric matrix through a sequence of plane rotations, each one zeroing an off-diagonal element. He applied it to astronomical problems computed by hand. The method was rediscovered for electronic computers in the 1950s and is still valued for its accuracy, because rotations do not amplify rounding errors.
\end{didyouknow}
